& [RequiredTransformation]
  + create a new bounded Cantor kernel crate rather than copying or admitting cantor_scribe wholesale
  + retain semantic data forms normalization domain-separated SHA256 generation manifest validation three-valued expressions exact source spans diagnostics and partial document analysis
  + adapt the fault type to remove SQLite and ambient I/O conversions from the kernel surface
  + require strict supplied machine forms including duplicate-set refusal where sets carry semantic identity
  + preserve the live source hashes and attribution while allowing reviewed refactoring needed for an effect-free kernel boundary

& [Excluded]
  + no SQLite storage schema filesystem project loading temp directory process identity environment LSP MCP Tokio network provider CLI or effect surface
  + no wholesale crate copy no mutation of the live C checkout and no claim that prior Eclipse tests alone prove Cantor kernel compatibility
  + no live model llama.cpp provider installation update remote machine FPGA or Minecraft work

& [AcceptanceIntent]
  + deterministic pure semantic analysis and validation under constructive and adversarial fixtures
  + static absence of process filesystem network environment database async transport provider and unsafe surfaces
  + exact component admission through the published instance-foundation contract only after its own SJS formation verification
